meta {
  name: Request Avatar Upload URL
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/me/avatar-upload
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "contentType": "image/jpeg",
    "contentLength": 48213
  }
}

docs {
  Returns a presigned PUT url, the key to attach afterwards, and the limits.
  Expect 200 with uploadUrl, key, expiresInSeconds (300) and maxBytes.

  Image bytes never pass through this server. Upload directly:

    curl -X PUT --data-binary @avatar.jpg \
      -H "Content-Type: image/jpeg" "<uploadUrl>"

  Then attach it with Update Profile, sending {"avatarKey": "<key>"}.

  Two things must match the values you declared here or R2 answers 403 with
  SignatureDoesNotMatch and no useful diagnostic: the Content-Type header,
  byte for byte, and the body length. contentLength is signed into the url
  precisely because it is the only size cap a presigned PUT can carry.

  Do NOT send an Authorization header on the PUT — it conflicts with the
  query-string credentials and R2 rejects it.
}
